<div class="deliverable reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Website &amp; search review</h3><p>We start by understanding where you stand: how your site is built, which searches already bring visitors, and where the gaps are. The review shapes everything that follows.</p></div>
<div class="deliverable reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Keyword and content planning</h3><p>We map the searches your customers actually make to the pages that should answer them — and plan the content those pages need. No keyword stuffing, no guesswork: useful pages for real questions.</p></div>
<div class="deliverable reveal"><span>03</span><h3>On-page optimisation</h3><p>Titles, descriptions, headings, internal links and page structure, tuned so search engines — and people — can tell what each page is about. If your site needs technical fixes, our <a href="/expertise-web-development/">web development team</a> handles them.</p></div>
<div class="deliverable reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Performance review</h3><p>Regular reviews of rankings, traffic and enquiries, explained in plain language. You will know what improved, what did not, and what we are doing next — and why.</p></div>
<p class="caption">Your project scope, deliverables and timeline are agreed after our first conversation.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">WHO IT’S FOR</span><h2>Who this service is for</h2><p>SEO suits any business whose customers search before they buy — which is most of them. We work with companies that want steady, long-term visibility rather than a one-off spike, and it pairs naturally with <a href="/digital-marketing/">digital marketing</a> for businesses that also want paid reach.</p></div>
<div class="values">
<article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Real estate</h3><p>Local and project-based search, so buyers find your developments when they search an area or a property type.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>E-commerce</h3><p>Product and category pages that show up for the searches shoppers actually make.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Healthcare</h3><p>Trustworthy, accurate pages for treatments and services, written for patients and their families.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Education</h3><p>Course and admission pages that reach students and parents comparing their options.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>05</span><h3>B2B &amp; industrial</h3><p>Specialist content that reaches buyers researching a product or supplier long before they enquire.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>06</span><h3>FMCG &amp; retail</h3><p>Brand and store visibility for the searches that happen before a purchase, online or in store.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</span><h2>Through our five-step process</h2><p>SEO is ongoing work, and it follows the same five-step process as everything we do — Discover, Plan, Build, Launch, Grow — with the emphasis on steady improvement rather than a single launch day.</p></div>
<div class="values">
<article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>Discover</h3><p>We learn how your customers search, what your competitors rank for, and where your site stands today.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>Plan</h3><p>A keyword and content plan, agreed with you, with clear priorities — the searches that matter most come first.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Pages optimised and new content created, with our <a href="/copyright/">copywriting team</a> writing for readers first and search engines second.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Launch</h3><p>Changes published carefully, so existing rankings are protected while new pages go live.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>05</span><h3>Grow</h3><p>Ongoing review and refinement: search behaviour changes, and your content should change with it.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">QUESTIONS</span><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
<div class="values">
<article class="reveal"><span>01</span><h3>What is SEO?</h3><p>Search engine optimisation is the work of making your website easy to find when people search for what you offer. It covers useful content, clear site structure, technical soundness and steady improvement over time.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>02</span><h3>How is SEO different from paid advertising?</h3><p>Paid ads buy visibility while you pay for it; SEO builds visibility that lasts. Many businesses use both — advertising for immediate reach, SEO for steady, long-term traffic.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>03</span><h3>How long does SEO take to show results?</h3><p>SEO is ongoing work, not a one-off fix. Some improvements show quickly; competitive searches take longer. We review progress regularly and explain what is changing, so you are never left guessing.</p></article>
<article class="reveal"><span>04</span><h3>Do you also create content for SEO?</h3><p>Yes. Useful content is at the heart of good SEO, and our copywriting team writes pages, guides and articles built around the searches your customers make.</p></article>
